// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Cocoon | per_page=5 | page=15 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T16:17:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				566,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Cocoon): Overhaul README with architecture, security, and project structure docs\n\nRewrite the Cocoon README from a brief overview into comprehensive project documentation covering:\n\n- **Key Features** — Fiber supervision, vscode API shimming, process hardening, code generation pipeline, multi-transport communications (gRPC, WebSocket, IPC), bidirectional streaming, telemetry, and the dual-layer debug server.\n- **Core Architecture Principles** — Fiber isolation, API surface parity, defense in depth, and transport flexibility, each with key component references.\n- **Project Structure** — Full directory tree under Element/Cocoon/ mapping every module to its purpose.\n- **Security** — Seven-layer security table documenting process hardening, exception boundaries, parent liveness monitoring, SecurityPolicy, runtime validation, module interception, WebSocket authentication, and memory enforcement, plus a forward-looking roadmap for platform-native sandboxing.\n- **Compatibility** — Integration matrix covering Grove, VS Code, Mountain, Sky, and Output.\n- **In the Land Project** — Updated comparison table for Cocoon vs Grove extension hosts.\n\nAlso updates package version references, reformats code/component names with backtick highlights, adds Grove and Mountain links to the Related Projects section, and applies FIDDEE-standard em-quad spacing between text and emoji icons throughout.\n\nAll existing content is preserved and expanded with no regressions in coverage.",
			"SHA": "611f5721f8c5d92fbc35c29ade5ba0f1bd37d64c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T15:12:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				566,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Cocoon): Strip superfluous blank lines from ESBuild.js\n\nRemove the vertical whitespace separating every export declaration, object property, and block statement in the ESBuild configuration module. The blank lines served no structural purpose and added unnecessary scrolling distance between related items.\n\nThis is the remainder of the formatting pass started in commit f0954fef — flattening all internal blank lines in Source/ESBuild.js for a denser, more scannable layout with no functional change.",
			"SHA": "a6494ff2525e17bedbbdf13cee56935e8b13ad2a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T15:11:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				566,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Cocoon): Ignore and remove tracked tsconfig.tsbuildinfo\n\nThe TypeScript incremental compilation cache (tsconfig.tsbuildinfo) was accidentally tracked in version control, causing spurious diffs on every build. Add the file to .gitignore and delete the tracked copy.\n\nThis aligns with the existing policy of not tracking transient build artifacts in the Cocoon workspace.",
			"SHA": "07586138898763d72ad7ff04e2f341f84336a966"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T14:36:05Z",
